# {{projectName}} — Windsurf Rules

## BLOCKING Rules
1. No `any` type — use `unknown` + type guards
2. No direct DB calls from UI — use convex queries/mutations
3. No business logic in components — extract to features/ hooks or convex functions
4. Features in `features/{name}/` — vertical slices with components/, hooks/, index.ts
5. Shared UI only in `components/` — ui/ for primitives, layout/ for shells
6. Convex validators required — `args` + `returns` on every query/mutation
7. Bounded reads — `.take(n)` or pagination, never unbounded `.collect()`
8. Index-backed queries — `.withIndex()`, no `.filter()` on full scans
9. Tests pass before merge — `pnpm test && pnpm typecheck`

## Stack
- Next.js 15+ (App Router, Server Components, Turbopack)
- Convex (reactive backend)
- Tailwind CSS v4
- next-intl (i18n)
- TypeScript strict

## Structure
- `app/[locale]/` — pages (route groups: marketing, auth, dashboard)
- `components/` — shared UI (ui/, layout/, providers/)
- `features/` — vertical slices (components/, hooks/, index.ts)
- `convex/` — backend (domain folders: schemas.ts, queries.ts, mutations.ts)
- `lib/` — utilities
- `i18n/` + `messages/` — internationalization

## Convex Patterns
- Domain folders: `convex/{domain}/schemas.ts + queries.ts + mutations.ts`
- Dual validators: data validator + document validator (with _id, _creationTime)
- Queries: `.withIndex()` + `.take(n)` + `args` + `returns`
- Mutations: `internalMutation` for sensitive ops, `.withIndex()` for lookups
- Schema: import domain tables into root `convex/schema.ts`

## features/ Pattern
- Each feature = self-contained vertical slice
- Public API via `index.ts` barrel export
- Consumers import from `@/features/{name}` only
- Never import feature internals directly

## Next.js Conventions
- Server Components default, `'use client'` when needed
- Data via convex hooks (useQuery/useMutation) in client components
- Route groups `(name)` for layout segmentation
- Middleware handles locale routing
